<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paxton Boys</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1763–1764</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Paxton Boys were frontier settlers from around Paxton in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennsylvania">Pennsylvania</a> who, during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pontiac">Pontiac</a>'s War, attacked the peaceful Conestoga Indians, survivors of the Susquehannock, in December 1763, killing all of them, including those sheltered in the Lancaster workhouse. In 1764 they marched on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philadelphia">Philadelphia</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benjamin-franklin">Benjamin Franklin</a> helped persuade them to turn back. None were punished.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paxton-boys.jpg" alt="Paxton Boys" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paxton_massacre.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
